        <dc:title>Food for Thought: Eighteen Talks on the Training of the Heart</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Dhammadharo, Ajaan Lee" opf:role="aut">Ajaan Lee Dhammadharo</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (4.9.1) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2012-03-05T08:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>This book is an introduction to the Buddhist practice of training the heart. It is taken from the talks of Phra Ajaan Lee Dhammadharo, a teacher in the Thai forest tradition of meditation, and is called "Food for Thought" because it invites the reader to fill in the spaces suggested by the talks -- to reflect on how the images and teachings they contain relate to one another and to one’s own situation in life.</dc:description>
